<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vincent of Saragossa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 304</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Saint Vincent the Deacon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vincent of Saragossa was a deacon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> who was martyred at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in the persecution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a>, around 304. He became one of the most widely venerated saints of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert I</a> brought back relics of him from Spain and founded an abbey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> to house them, later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-germain-des-pres">Saint-Germain-des-Prés</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vincent-of-saragossa.jpg" alt="Vincent of Saragossa" width="320" height="516" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomás Giner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vicente_de_Zaragoza_by_Tom%C3%A1s_Giner,_1462%E2%80%931466.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
